WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
72 Mangeses ordered to save Hamakua Cain, later hunted Hawaiian ground birds. This is Unintended

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:11.940
Consequences, Episode 142. Sugar planters on the Hamakua coast of Hawaii Island were

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.100
watching a crop disappear in the early 1880s. Rats stripped Cain until whole sections

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:23.217
became unharvestable. The fields were not thinning at the edges. Contemporary accounts described

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:28.917
populations in the hundreds of thousands, breeding in newly planted Cain. Pacific Sugar Mill

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.717
had already lost entire fields.

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:34.657
For a mill, an unharvestable section is not a wildlife story.

00:00:35.097 --> 00:00:37.217
It is tonnage that never reaches the rollers.

00:00:37.777 --> 00:00:42.317
The men who ran those plantations faced a concrete economic threat, and they looked

00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:45.097
for a response that would not have to be repeated every night.

00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.757
Traping and poisoning had already been tried.

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:51.537
Both were labor intensive, and both were only partly effective.

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:57.037
Workers could patrol, set traps, and lay poison, and the rats kept breeding in the cane.

00:00:57.037 --> 00:01:05.357
A single hunter that covered ground on its own looked on that ledger, like a better bargain than a crew that had to be paid to walk the same rows again.

00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:09.157
The animal they had in mind was the small Indian mongoose.

00:01:09.697 --> 00:01:17.497
Planners had seen mongoose's succeed against rats on Jamaican plantations, and they believed the same animal would do the same work in Hawaiian cane.

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:22.717
W.H. Purvis brought the first animals from India and Africa in 1883.

00:01:23.477 --> 00:01:28.377
Joseph Marsden, later known as Mongoose Joe, arranged a larger shipment from Jamaica

00:01:28.377 --> 00:01:29.257
that same year.

00:01:29.777 --> 00:01:30.617
The hope was simple.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:35.197
The animals would hunt the rodents the way they had in the Caribbean, and the cane would

00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:36.597
stand long enough to be cut.

00:01:37.177 --> 00:01:39.837
No one conducted formal tests of the broader diet.

00:01:40.357 --> 00:01:43.577
No one tested whether the animals would stay inside the cane fields.

00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:46.117
That absence was not a secret loophole.

00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:51.517
It followed from the era's view that agricultural improvements were private matters, best settled

00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:52.917
by the plantations themselves.

00:01:53.557 --> 00:01:57.117
There was no regulatory review standing between an order and a release.

00:01:57.777 --> 00:02:00.277
The logic as the planters held it was straightforward.

00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:02.217
Rats destroyed revenue.

00:02:02.857 --> 00:02:03.777
Mungoosa's eight rats.

00:02:04.177 --> 00:02:05.117
The fields would recover.

00:02:05.637 --> 00:02:09.777
They weighed lost tonnage against the cost of campaigns that had already failed to finish

00:02:09.777 --> 00:02:10.237
the job.

00:02:10.777 --> 00:02:15.177
The animals were expected to breed and hold their own numbers, so the plantation would not

00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:20.157
have to keep buying replacements. Because the sugar companies operated on narrow margins tied

00:02:20.157 --> 00:02:25.857
to global prices, any drop in rodent damage translated directly into acres that could be milled

00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:31.237
instead of left standing. A mongoose that needed no nightly wage and no further shipment once it

00:02:31.237 --> 00:02:37.017
was breeding looked like a self-sustaining fix for a repeating loss. That is the decision as it sat

00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:42.937
in 1883. A small group of sugarmen, a crop they could not harvest, and an animal that had already

00:02:42.937 --> 00:02:44.597
earned a reputation somewhere else.

00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:48.097
The Jamaica Shipmen arrived in Hilo in 1883.

00:02:49.206 --> 00:02:52.426
The animals were released along the Hamakua and Hilo coasts.

00:02:52.926 --> 00:02:56.906
Planters on Maui, Malokai, and Oahu soon asked for their own shipments.

00:02:57.606 --> 00:03:01.286
Offspring from the original group were carried to those islands within a few years.

00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:06.666
The same ships that took mild sugar to market came back with more animals when neighbors requested

00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:06.906
them.

00:03:07.466 --> 00:03:11.846
That made a low friction network across the islands that already had active plantations.

00:03:11.846 --> 00:03:16.746
distributions. Distribution did not require a new institution. It rode the routes the sugar

00:03:16.746 --> 00:03:22.066
trade already used. Planta's track success the way a mill tracks a season. They compared

00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:25.066
yields on the same fields before and after the introduction.

00:03:25.746 --> 00:03:31.286
Sections once written off as total losses began producing measurable tons per acre. Newspaper

00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:36.646
reports from 1898 noted that rat eaten cane had become almost unknown on properties that

00:03:36.646 --> 00:03:38.686
had once considered abandoning cultivation.

00:03:39.526 --> 00:03:44.726
H.A. Baldwin of Maui wrote in 1921 that the change was dramatic enough to save entire

00:03:44.726 --> 00:03:45.226
harvests.

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:48.646
Those reports are the voice of the people who ordered the animals.

00:03:49.246 --> 00:03:51.306
On their measure, the introduction was working.

00:03:51.906 --> 00:03:54.866
The animals required no ongoing feed and no housing.

00:03:55.426 --> 00:04:00.006
The recurring cost was the initial purchase and the transport, and that cost was recovered

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.386
once rat pressure dropped.

00:04:01.386 --> 00:04:06.906
For a business living on the margin between a global price and a local harvest, a one-time

00:04:06.906 --> 00:04:09.906
outlay that then maintained itself was the outcome they had bought.

00:04:10.486 --> 00:04:12.686
The Mongooses did take rodents in the cane.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.366
They also did not remain a plantation tool.

00:04:15.926 --> 00:04:21.186
They spread on their own beyond the fields, into grasslands and forests, and up to 7,000 feet

00:04:21.186 --> 00:04:21.766
in elevation.

00:04:22.486 --> 00:04:23.966
No agency required testing.

00:04:24.586 --> 00:04:26.206
No agency required quarantine.

00:04:26.826 --> 00:04:29.826
The releases were treated as ordinary agricultural practice.

00:04:29.826 --> 00:04:34.646
the same category as a new variety of cane or a change in how a field was planted.

00:04:35.026 --> 00:04:38.706
There is no record in this story of a formal descent at the moment of release.

00:04:39.743 --> 00:04:45.583
The skepticism that matters here arrived later from naturalists who could see what the yield sheets did not record,

00:04:46.043 --> 00:04:49.103
and from dock workers who would one day refuse a further shipment.

00:04:49.743 --> 00:04:53.523
At the time of the Hilo release, the measure of success was cane that could be cut.

00:04:54.003 --> 00:04:56.783
By that measure, the early decades looked like a success.

00:04:56.783 --> 00:05:02.243
the same animals that cut rat damage in the fields proved opportunistic once they left them.

00:05:02.823 --> 00:05:08.563
Scat studies and field observations later documented predation on eggs and hatchlings. The list is

00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:16.363
specific, Nene, Hawaiian petrels, Nual's shear waters, Koloa, IAO, other ground nesting species

00:05:16.363 --> 00:05:22.623
besides. The birds nested on the ground. During molt, they remained flightless. A nest on the ground,

00:05:22.623 --> 00:05:27.403
and a bird that cannot lift off is an additional food source for a hunter already moving through

00:05:27.403 --> 00:05:28.083
that habitat.

00:05:28.483 --> 00:05:33.263
The dietary flexibility that made a mongoose useful against rats and cane also let

00:05:33.263 --> 00:05:37.843
it switch when rodent numbers fluctuated with the season, or when nests became easier

00:05:37.843 --> 00:05:39.563
to find in that flightless period.

00:05:40.103 --> 00:05:42.463
The importers had not anticipated that switch.

00:05:42.983 --> 00:05:45.743
Their calculations stopped at the rodent and the ton of cane.

00:05:46.363 --> 00:05:51.303
The animals established on Hawaii Island, on Maui, on Malokai, and on Oahu.

00:05:51.303 --> 00:05:53.703
They never reached Kauai or Lanai.

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:58.803
On the islands where they did establish, Nanei nest success in monitored areas fell to

00:05:58.803 --> 00:06:01.123
roughly 58-62%.

00:06:01.123 --> 00:06:05.063
On Mangu's free Kauai, nest success stood at 82%.

00:06:05.343 --> 00:06:08.843
The same pattern touched at least 8 federally listed Hawaiian birds.

00:06:09.383 --> 00:06:13.063
That gap is not a coincidence of weather or of one bad nesting year.

00:06:13.603 --> 00:06:16.863
It tracks the presence of a predator the cane fields had invited in.

00:06:17.383 --> 00:06:19.723
The causal chain is short enough to say plainly.

00:06:19.723 --> 00:06:23.023
An industry decision was made without dietary screening.

00:06:23.603 --> 00:06:25.903
Animals were released at multiple coastal points.

00:06:26.323 --> 00:06:30.803
They followed corridors of grassland and forest edge that already connected the plantations

00:06:30.803 --> 00:06:31.863
to higher ground.

00:06:32.563 --> 00:06:34.023
Nane nested in those uplands.

00:06:34.603 --> 00:06:39.443
Each additional island then held its own breeding population, and that population's growth

00:06:39.443 --> 00:06:42.303
was no longer limited by the original plantation fence.

00:06:42.943 --> 00:06:46.403
Second order, fledgling production fell across more than one species.

00:06:46.403 --> 00:06:47.263
3.

00:06:47.443 --> 00:06:52.903
Third order, the archipelago split into lasting zones, islands with an established Mongoose population

00:06:52.903 --> 00:06:54.323
and islands without one.

00:06:54.843 --> 00:06:59.503
The planter's ledger never included that split because the ledger stopped at Cain tonnage.

00:07:00.043 --> 00:07:04.783
Kawai's higher nest success was real, and it was never part of the 1883 arithmetic.

00:07:05.503 --> 00:07:09.443
Nothing in the purchase order asked what else lived on the ground between the mill and the

00:07:09.443 --> 00:07:10.123
upland nests.

00:07:10.723 --> 00:07:15.023
By the early 20th century, naturalists could already see the damage to native birds.

00:07:15.023 --> 00:07:20.003
words. The sugar industry looking at harvests continued to treat the mongoose as a net benefit

00:07:20.003 --> 00:07:24.943
for cane. Both readings could be true at once. The fields had been saved on the measure

00:07:24.943 --> 00:07:29.983
that justified the order. The birds were paying a cost that measure never priced. State

00:07:29.983 --> 00:07:35.243
law later classified the animal as injurious wildlife. Current rules prohibit import

00:07:35.243 --> 00:07:40.503
keeping or breeding except under permit. That is a redesign aimed at the border, not at

00:07:40.503 --> 00:07:42.603
populations already breeding in the forests.

00:07:43.363 --> 00:07:48.223
Kauai and Lani remained free of established populations largely because a planned shipment

00:07:48.223 --> 00:07:52.903
to Kauai was thrown overboard by dock workers, and no later release succeeded.

00:07:53.503 --> 00:07:56.323
Those workers are the clearest human interruption in the record.

00:07:56.803 --> 00:07:59.643
They did not reverse what had already landed on the other islands.

00:08:00.183 --> 00:08:02.543
They stopped one more island from joining the list.

00:08:03.103 --> 00:08:08.843
Ongoing control focuses on preventing new arrivals, not on eradication across the four colonized

00:08:08.843 --> 00:08:09.223
islands.

00:08:09.223 --> 00:08:14.523
Modern management treats those four islands as permanently altered. Resources go to

00:08:14.523 --> 00:08:19.843
keeping the remaining two clean. Inspection of incoming cargo and a rapid response if someone

00:08:19.843 --> 00:08:25.723
reports a sighting. No reversal of the original releases is possible. The Nane population has

00:08:25.723 --> 00:08:31.203
rebounded from a few dozen birds to more than 4,000, and the majority of those birds are now on

00:08:31.203 --> 00:08:38.063
Kauai. The gap in nesting success between Mongoose-free islands and Mongoose-present islands persists. Recovery

00:08:38.063 --> 00:08:42.463
Every on Kauai shows that the absence of this one predator can shift breeding outcomes in

00:08:42.463 --> 00:08:43.763
a way managers can measure.

00:08:44.303 --> 00:08:48.723
The same record also shows that cats and disease continue to limit numbers even where

00:08:48.723 --> 00:08:49.923
mongooses are absent.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:52.843
Removing one pressure does not clear the ledger.

00:08:53.263 --> 00:08:55.603
It reveals the other pressures that were always there.

00:08:56.163 --> 00:08:57.883
The meta-irony sits in the geography.

00:08:58.603 --> 00:09:04.163
The animal was ordered as a cheap self-sustaining control, expected to breed and hold its numbers

00:09:04.163 --> 00:09:05.383
without further shipments.

00:09:05.383 --> 00:09:08.263
That is exactly what it did, on four islands.

00:09:08.843 --> 00:09:11.703
Past the point where anyone still wanted the breeding to continue.

00:09:12.691 --> 00:09:16.611
The trait that made the purchase rational in a mill office is the trait that made the

00:09:16.611 --> 00:09:18.271
outcome permanent in the uplands.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:23.511
The Hamakua planters chose a predator whose diet had not been measured against the full set

00:09:23.511 --> 00:09:25.131
of prey on the islands they managed.

00:09:25.771 --> 00:09:27.831
They were not guessing in the dark about rats.

00:09:28.431 --> 00:09:29.351
They had lost fields.

00:09:29.931 --> 00:09:31.391
They had watched trapping fail.

00:09:31.391 --> 00:09:35.471
They had a Caribbean precedent and a price that punished every lost ton.

00:09:36.191 --> 00:09:40.031
What they did not weigh was everything the Mongoose might eat once it left the Rose.

00:09:40.671 --> 00:09:45.571
When an agricultural decision rewarded only short-term rat reduction, the longer effect

00:09:45.571 --> 00:09:48.691
on ground-nesting birds received no weight in the calculation.

00:09:49.531 --> 00:09:53.311
Later regulators did not try to unwind four established populations.

00:09:53.891 --> 00:09:58.351
They drew strict geographic lines around the islands that were still free, and they put

00:09:58.351 --> 00:10:03.831
the force of law on import, keeping, and breeding. The response matched what was still reversible.

00:10:04.451 --> 00:10:09.891
A shipment can be refused. A breeding population in forest up to the high country cannot be called

00:10:09.891 --> 00:10:16.647
back. The pattern is the unmeasured interaction becoming the lasting cost. A single economic metric

00:10:16.647 --> 00:10:21.907
stood in for an entire ecological ledger, and the items left off that metric are the ones still

00:10:21.907 --> 00:10:26.947
shaping which islands can raise ground birds at the higher rate. Environmental intelligence

00:10:26.947 --> 00:10:31.567
covers the regulatory side. The question worth carrying out of this case is not whether

00:10:31.567 --> 00:10:35.787
sugar should have been saved. The planters were answering a real loss with the tools

00:10:35.787 --> 00:10:40.647
and the information their business recognized. The question is what a pest management choice

00:10:40.647 --> 00:10:45.647
counts before it is allowed to breed on its own. If the invoice names only the crop and

00:10:45.647 --> 00:10:50.547
the pest, the species that share the ground never enter the sum, and they cannot be added

00:10:50.547 --> 00:10:55.387
later at the same price. How do current pest management choices weight the species that

00:10:55.387 --> 00:10:57.087
that are not part of the original invoice.

